        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 2055,
        "paragraph_id": "506B9B78",
        "text": "The predictor-corrector set is second order accurate in regions where the solution is smooth, and reduces locally to first order accuracy near discontinuities. Furthermore, the method remains mass conservative. Note that other flux limiters can be used instead of the minmod limiter. However, as the minmod limiter performed adequately, this has not been investigated. (for an overview of flux limiters see Hirsch, 2007)"
